==Battleground==
*1 [[Teacher Cybear]] spawns as the boss after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because Teacher Cybear has 600 range and deals 999,999 damage per hit, he annihilates almost any cat in the game. However, he only hits a single target with each attack and is not assisted by any other enemy units, meaning that the HP and level of your units are completely irrelevant.

The best strategy is to spam any and all cheap (75/150¢ cost) meatshields you have. That includes but is not limited to: [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]], [[Awa-Odori Cat (Rare Cat)|Awa-Odori Cat]], etc. Again, health doesn't matter, so pick the cheapest meatshields you have. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] is also useful as its Metal ability allows it to deny 12 attacks from this enemy. It is also recommended you use rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] as soon as Cybear's gone so you can immediately claim your reward.

As Teacher Cybear attacks once every second and the lowest possible recharge time for a meatshield is 2 seconds, you will need a minimum of three meatshields to permanently stall him. However, you will then need a fourth meatshield in order to start whittling away his health. Usage of Worker Cat Start Level UP or Starting Money UP [[Cat Combo]]s will keep a steady flow of meatshields, stopping Teacher Cybear in place and making the stage go by much faster, but it's still doable without them.

